 (out/'10_Explainability/GRADCAM_METHOD.md').write_text('''# Standard Grad-CAM implementation\n\nReference: https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.02391 . This is standard gradient-weighted CAM, not Grad-CAM++, Score-CAM, Eigen-CAM or a segmentation method. For predicted raw logit z_c and final spatial stage feature A_k, compute alpha_k=(1/HW)sum_uv d z_c/d A_k(u,v), then CAM=ReLU(sum_k alpha_k A_k). Normalize each image independently to[0,1] and bilinearly upsample to224×224. Overlay is60%original RGB+40%magma map. Color scales are relative within each image, not calibrated importance or comparable absolute saliency across cases.\n\nAll six selected real trained checkpoints are used. For each true class/model, choose the correct and incorrect validation example nearest median saved top1 confidence; tie by image ID. Classify/explain the actual predicted class, not the ground-truth class. Reuse the original contiguous validation batch, size16(or8forConvNeXt-Tiny), normalization and CUDA BF16 autocast; verify same top1 and max absolute probability difference<=0.02 before accepting a map. All48canonical cases matched all four saved probabilities exactly (max difference0). Float32 gradient aggregation is applied after BF16 forward/autograd. Teacher/extra-loss modules are absent from enhanced inference.\n\nThe targeted stage is blocks.last for MobileNet/EfficientNet and stages.last for ConvNeXt, always spatial7×7 rather than pooled1×1. Exact module paths, feature dimensions, raw normalized spatial CSV maps, upsampled NPY maps, checkpoint/input hashes and original batch IDs are saved. Only approved validation images are read for explanations; source copies include supporting validation batches. Models run eval with parameter gradients disabled; only input/feature gradients are computed, without optimizer or parameter updates.\n\nAn initial CPU FP32 attempt is retained as a diagnostic:13of48cases exceeded probability parity tolerance, despite matching labels. Its partial figures are not publication figures. Canonical CUDA BF16 maps supersede that attempt. Qualitative maps do not establish clinical feature use, faithfulness, robustness, absence of bias, or localization accuracy. No lesion masks/localization metric were evaluated and no XAI was integrated into Flutter.\n''')
 (data/'IMAGE_ATTRIBUTION_AND_ACCESS.md').write_text('''# Image attribution and permitted access\n\nISIC2019 research samples are drawn from the official challenge training-source release, which contains BCN20000/Hospital Clínic de Barcelona, HAM10000/ViDIR Medical University of Vienna and MSK contributions. Retain the official dataset citations and CC BY-NC4.0 attribution/noncommercial terms: https://challenge.isic-archive.com/data/#2019 . Existing repository DATASETS.md records the source/terms. Ground-truth labels and selected paths/hashes come exclusively from approved release v20261117T060846Z_608314c8.\n\nThe representative/preprocessing panels use eight illustrative eligible training images (four raw before/after pairs). They are seed-42 examples, not claimed statistically representative or diagnostic guidance. Standard Grad-CAM uses48selected validation targets and their approved validation-batch context. Input assets are byte-identical copies of prepared validation JPEGs and selected raw training sources. No ISIC test or PAD image is opened or copied. Those partitions appear only as metadata totals.\n''')
 (out/'README.md').write_text('# '+TITLE+'\n\n# Complete training/validation publication package\n\nVersion `'+out.name+'`; immutable approved dataset `'+RELEASE.name+'`. Start with TRAINING_RESULTS_REPORT.md, FIGURE_INDEX.csv and FIGURE_CAPTIONS.md. There are **'+str(len(records))+' canonical figures** (three export formats each); six preliminary CPU XAI figure families are archived diagnostics, not counted or published.\n\n## Folder structure\n\n'+ '\n'.join('- `'+d+'`: '+description for d,description in zip(CATEGORIES,['Scope, main report and availability table.','Training distribution, metadata split sizes, imbalance, illustrative samples and original/prepared pairs.','Actual-code major-stage architecture schematics; training-only teacher/student modules.','Per-run losses, accuracy, macro-F1, validation macro-F1 and exact LR curves.','Six raw and six row-percent confusion matrices, consistent all-model/focused comparisons.','Six one-vs-rest ROC and six per-class PR figures, macro AUROC/AP comparisons.','Precision/recall/F1, sensitivities, targeted errors, support and false positives.','Aggregate metrics, grouped horizontal comparison, paired metric deltas and epoch budgets.','Parameter/MAC profiles, full checkpoint sizes, measured times/VRAM and parameter-F1 scatter.','Training gates, recorded LR loss components and original/control curves.','Canonical validation-only standard Grad-CAM and method description.','All source tables, copied run histories/probabilities/logs/configs, all105epoch checkpoints, six selected shortcuts, sample/CAM assets, exact generator/training code and environment locks.','Flat copies of every canonical PNG/SVG/PDF, with the same index and captions.']))+'\n\n## Checkpoints and data\n\nAll selected checkpoints are byte-identical copies in11_Source_Data/checkpoints. All105epoch payloads are copied to11_Source_Data/recorded_runs/<model>/checkpoints and audited by complete_checkpoint_inventory.csv. This duplicates no training and changes no original file. The package is intentionally large because it contains actual checkpoints and probabilities, not just rendered figures. No dataset image collection is copied wholesale: only permitted sample/XAI assets are included. Archived paths in tables preserve original provenance; package-relative paths permit direct access to copied records.\n\n## Reproduce without training\n\nUse the existing project .venv and the exact scripts saved in11_Source_Data/generation_scripts. Work from the repository root, or set MOBILESKINXAI_PROJECT_ROOT to its absolute path. `build.py init` creates a NEW unique output directory. Run phases prepare, plots, models, xai, finish with `--output <new_directory>`; xai uses CUDA BF16 and only approved validation batches. No phase invokes training, downloads weights, exports TFLite, evaluates test/PAD, or modifies Flutter. The same runtime packages are recorded in environment.json and requirements_generation.lock.txt. Selected recorded probabilities are used unchanged for ROC/PR; image inference is limited to CAM validation cases. Existing figure outputs are not silently overwritten.\n\nThe CPU `models_xai.xai` helper is retained only to reproduce the archived FP32 diagnostic attempt; the canonical build xai phase uses xai_cuda.generate. Each FIGURE_INDEX row names its data files, source hashes, split, method and exact script. Run definitions and original/LR training implementations are saved for provenance, not to be executed by this package.\n\n## Export and limitations\n\nPNG files are300DPI; SVG/PDF preserve vector text/lines/shapes, with photographs and heatmaps embedded as raster where required. Full model names and requested palette are used. Publication figures do not claim independent clinical performance or original methodology; the only diagrams are requested code-derived architecture abstractions. No mobile latency/XAI-in-Flutter claim is made. See the report for adaptive validation reuse, class imbalance, selection/budget and patient-independence limitations. Do not treat these validation scores as locked-test generalization.\n')
